#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068840 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068447 :question/id #uuid "d1de6657-82b1-5bcb-b8cc-fd2629d31faa" :question/math-academy-id "e-10832" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y' = \\dfrac {x^2}{y}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y} \\\\ y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}y^2 = \\dfrac{1}{3}x^3 + C.\n$$\n\nWe can express the solution in the form $y = y(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+C \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+2C \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+2C} \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+K}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K = 2C.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f0876a-33f0-5c6b-9195-8b9a0a550655" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671874 :question-generator/id #uuid "b3dbf88a-2512-5834-bad2-4223c41b025d" :question-generator/script "generators/89/89015ef9fd221785f4ba65ced7fbce8b46a46b5219335ed046db08d45e044791/17592186068840.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069061 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "184d638d-4f43-5a61-a9aa-986f3a8d0dbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269471} {:answer/id #uuid "349a3566-02ae-5b67-8d72-7bd88977f0c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269751} {:answer/id #uuid "64f06b04-a151-5196-a323-0ff963707282" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270168} {:answer/id #uuid "a6629602-dc5e-5bc2-92b8-bcfffe8f083a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270759} {:answer/id #uuid "e7c59461-10cd-516c-bdd1-affc4f03909b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6629602-dc5e-5bc2-92b8-bcfffe8f083a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270759} :answer-field/id #uuid "783e5ec9-8d8f-5c4c-b6d1-cdb57257612e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271723}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "432fe98f-ffaf-5033-958e-d3cb37de9f8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-14244" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069062 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b657e03-7993-5721-9a5b-d80240b025be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}+y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269491} {:answer/id #uuid "4f6b4ac3-40cd-56f5-a8ef-2d1ffef6fc5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269985} {:answer/id #uuid "7464bda0-43dc-5fdf-8e19-585d1a9061ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270297} {:answer/id #uuid "a5d74015-a23f-5510-af78-69d656de3331" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270754} {:answer/id #uuid "bf138df5-1e52-57d6-bb9c-63f3bc95323c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f6b4ac3-40cd-56f5-a8ef-2d1ffef6fc5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269985} :answer-field/id #uuid "c282741d-f793-55ca-ac4d-c9a4c645b15f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271863}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c17c4aa5-1ffc-5c4e-9267-85cce391b502" :question/math-academy-id "q-14257" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}={y}^{2}+1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={y}^{2}+1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{2}+1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(y) & =x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(y)=x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+C).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235519 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2ab1da2-a1c8-5cce-81e3-77b494aca80e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-0.03t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2ab1da2-a1c8-5cce-81e3-77b494aca80e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-0.03t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234849} :answer-field/id #uuid "105ae6ea-d079-52d2-9fc8-366d8f97f343" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234985}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "39cc2ed4-7534-5355-9c68-129ad8345d1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-168077" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation in part 1 for $T\\ne 25.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $T\\,=\\,25+K\\cdot \\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,\\,$where $K$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we separate variables and integrate both sides with respect to $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t} & =-0.03(T-25) \\\\ \\frac{1}{T-25}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t} & =-0.03 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{T-25}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int -0.03\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}T}{T-25} & =-0.03\\int \\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|T-25| & =-0.03t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a perfectly valid general solution. However, if we want to write $T=T(t)$ explicitly, then we can solve for $T.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|T-25| & =-0.03t+C \\\\ |T-25| & ={e}^{-0.03t+C} \\\\ |T-25| & =K\\,{e}^{-0.03t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary positive constant.\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be both positive and negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =25+K\\,{e}^{-0.03t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275407 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46c59991-7a2a-5f22-a893-e1cd23ff3aae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272993} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc9c947-fac1-5eb0-93a8-ce473b0e579a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{2x+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273185} {:answer/id #uuid "6a59d67a-5461-5f00-bbb9-b66319e8bd0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{3}x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273304} {:answer/id #uuid "71bcc40b-d574-5391-8487-43c9455497a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=({x}^{2}+C)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273364} {:answer/id #uuid "e4680ae6-1495-57dd-a494-1cc9894aadf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=(\\sqrt[3]{x}+C)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274408}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46c59991-7a2a-5f22-a893-e1cd23ff3aae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272993} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ab142bb-121a-5834-81c7-b4ae5d3fdcbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274761}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "088db977-5f34-5d61-a165-97cdc5e6df38" :question/math-academy-id "q-158012" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{3{y}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2x}{3{y}^{2}} \\\\ 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {y}^{3} & ={x}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}={x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+C}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275408 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "019119ed-0828-5d14-913a-ecb47950b217" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272395} {:answer/id #uuid "0b63defe-eba9-54f7-8c7f-b0bba025e804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272491} {:answer/id #uuid "612cc7e3-fab2-5707-b558-c6527bd1837a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273228} {:answer/id #uuid "83e2e646-4e20-564b-867b-ae7e68e0f341" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273520} {:answer/id #uuid "a01c641c-59d0-5fde-8400-4b249323e3a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b63defe-eba9-54f7-8c7f-b0bba025e804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272491} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdbfba5c-9780-5693-999b-a9c027c35c8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275083}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "253f761f-d9dd-516e-a877-3691e4e75b8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-158013" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}$ for $y\\ne 0$ and $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<x<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={sec}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275409 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18e3c6b0-0e58-5c33-8744-40f2dcdff54e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272603} {:answer/id #uuid "78f4f93b-be8f-5c4d-a519-6d99d4fba770" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273424} {:answer/id #uuid "8883ebfa-4000-5edd-9354-c90407ee9c40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273559} {:answer/id #uuid "952e6dd1-43ff-54f6-9de1-fd7289574d4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273685} {:answer/id #uuid "e21a3412-a805-5477-baaf-507c3b52c7c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18e3c6b0-0e58-5c33-8744-40f2dcdff54e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272603} :answer-field/id #uuid "379ffcc8-e905-5697-a128-ee6a8efb7a2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274732}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c6ab8c9-fca1-56b1-82a8-98c4fa9f8c2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-158014" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275410 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "291a5622-7898-54ac-9d79-b2a74f3942f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{3}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272754} {:answer/id #uuid "319d04e8-d751-5e77-9108-47d7c52f477e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{2}/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272832} {:answer/id #uuid "465f3293-d914-56fa-982c-5e0bcdc0476d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{{x}^{2}/2}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272987} {:answer/id #uuid "59934890-57e8-5e1f-8f0a-10c08ef2b159" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={e}^{{x}^{3}/3}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273152} {:answer/id #uuid "cc14ee5c-23f4-50e2-8f50-91774b8a5ab3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "291a5622-7898-54ac-9d79-b2a74f3942f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=K{e}^{{x}^{3}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272754} :answer-field/id #uuid "7709ba3d-848c-528e-ad97-e70bdde49520" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274837}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4256446e-61ea-5cf5-ad92-3c95c9cc3119" :question/math-academy-id "q-158015" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}={x}^{2}y$ for $y\\ne 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={x}^{2}y \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =\\frac{1}{3}\\,{x}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|=\\frac{1}{3}\\,{x}^{3}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}/3+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{{x}^{3}/3}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ |y| & =K{e}^{{x}^{3}/3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K={e}^{C}$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K{e}^{{x}^{3}/3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275411 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #u